A note attaches to the end of the block before it, as a footnote mark
does. Figures are saved by \code{\link[=save_document]{save_document()}} at the size of their slot
with \code{\link[=save_figure_set]{save_figure_set()}}; see \code{\link[=figure_slide]{figure_slide()}} for \code{plot} and \code{name}, and
for how text is escaped (the same rules apply).

\code{document_table()} sets a data.frame, such as the output of
\code{\link[=report_table]{report_table()}}, as it is: column names become the head, numeric
columns are right-aligned and formatted with \code{\link[=format]{format()}}, negative numbers
get a minus sign, and every cell is escaped. Format numbers first (for
example with \code{\link[=format_estimate]{format_estimate()}}) to control their decimals.
